\":\"Sets `value` as the allowance of `spender` over ``owner``'s tokens,\\n     * given ``owner``'s signed approval.\\n     *\\n     * IMPORTANT: The same issues {IERC20-approve} has related to transaction\\n     * ordering also applies here.\\n     *\\n     * Emits an {Approval} event.\\n     *\\n     * Requirements:\\n     *\\n     * - `spender` cannot be the zero address.\\n     * - `deadline` must be a timestamp in the future.\\n     * - `v`, `r` and `s` must be a valid `secp256k1` signature from `owner`\\n     * over the EIP712-formatted function arguments.\\n     * - the signature must use ``owner``'s current nonce (see {nonces}).\\n     *\\n     * For more information on the signature format, see the\\n     * EIP-2612 specification.\\n     *\\n     * CAUTION: See Security Considerations above.\\n     \"},\"nonces(address)\":{\"details\":\"Returns the current nonce for `owner`. This value must be\\n     * included whenever a signature is generated for {permit}.\\n     *\\n     * Every successful call to {permit} increases ``owner``'s nonce by one. This\\n     * prevents a signature from being used multiple times.\\n     \"},\"DOMAIN_SEPARATOR()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the domain separator used in the encoding of the signature for {permit}, as defined by {EIP712}.\\n     \"},\"sharesOf(address)\":{\"details\":\"Shares are constant between mint/burn operations.\\n     *      balanceOf() is computed as sharesOf * redemptionRate.\",\"params\":{\"account\":\"The address to query\"},\"returns\":{\"shares\":\"The underlying share balance\\n     \"}},\"totalShares()\":{\"details\":\"Shares are constant between mint/burn. `totalSupply()` is the zapout of\\n     *      protocol-owned reserve LP (bond NFT), not `totalShares * 1`.\",\"returns\":{\"shares\":\"Total underlying shares\\n     \"}},\"redemptionRate()\":{\"details\":\"Quote is `previewClaimLiquidity` of protocol-owned originalShares (token id 0),\\n     *      i.e. single-sided zapout of that LP from the reserve pool. `balanceOf` is\\n     *      the holder's pro-rata slice of that zapout.\",\"returns\":{\"rate\":\"settlement-token value per share (1e18 precision)\\n     \"}},\"detf()\":{\"returns\":{\"_0\":\"The DETF diamond\\n     \"}},\"setDetf(address)\":{\"details\":\"Owner-only deployment-time wiring hook for composed DETF deployments.\",\"params\":{\"detf\":\"The DETF contract\\n     \"}},\"detfNFTId()\":{\"returns\":{\"_0\":\"The protocol NFT token ID\\n     \"}},\"rateAsset()\":{\"details\":\"The method name remains `rateAsset()` for compatibility with existing callers.\\n    *      Deployments may use any configured common token, not only rateAsset.\",\"returns\":{\"_0\":\"The configured common token\\n     \"}},\"convertToShares(uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"rebasingClaimAmount\":\"Amount of rebasing claim token\"},\"returns\":{\"shares\":\"Equivalent underlying shares\\n     \"}},\"convertToClaim(uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"shares\":\"Amount of shares\"},\"returns\":{\"rebasingClaimAmount\":\"Equivalent rebasing claim token amount\\n     \"}},\"previewRedeem(uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"rebasingClaimAmount\":\"Amount of rebasing claim token to redeem\"},\"returns\":{\"wethOut\":\"Amount of configured common token that would be received\\n     \"}},\"updateRedemptionRate()\":{\"details\":\"Permissionless poke; no-op when rate is unchanged.\\n     \"},\"mintFromNFTSale(uint256,address)\":{\"details\":\"Called by the DETF diamond when users sell their NFTs.\\n     *      LP shares are transferred to the protocol NFT held by this contract.\",\"params\":{\"lpShares\":\"Amount of LP shares being contributed\",\"recipient\":\"Address to receive rebasing claim token\"},\"returns\":{\"rebasingClaimMinted\":\"Amount of rebasing claim token minted\\n     \"}},\"mintFromNFTSale(uint256,uint256,address)\":{\"details\":\"`totalAssetsBefore == type(uint256).max` means live-read `originalSharesOf(detfNFTId)`\\n     *      (safe only when the credit has not landed yet — `buyClaim`). Sell must pass the snapshot.\",\"params\":{\"assets\":\"BPT credited this call.\",\"totalAssetsBefore\":\"Protocol NFT originalShares before this credit, or `type(uint256).max`.\",\"recipient\":\"Address to receive rebasing claim token.\\n     \"}},\"redeem(uint256,address,bool)\":{\"details\":\"Compatibility wrapper around the canonical `exchangeIn(rebasing claim token -> common token)` path.\\n    *      Always redeemable - no price gate. rebasing claim token represents a claim on the\\n    *      protocol-owned NFT's reserve-pool BPT, and holders can exit at any time.\\n     *\\n     *      Process:\\n    *      1. Convert apparent rebasing claim token amount to internal shares\\n    *      2. Convert those shares into protocol-owned reserve-pool BPT claim\\n    *      3. Burn the rebasing claim token shares atomically\\n    *      4. Ask the DETF to claim/unwind that reserve-pool BPT into the configured common token\\n    *      5. Send the common token to the user\\n     *\",\"params\":{\"rebasingClaimAmount\":\"Amount of rebasing claim token to redeem\",\"recipient\":\"Address to receive the configured common token\",\"pretransferred\":\"Integrating-contract flag only. Callers with no bytecode revert `EOAPretransferNotAllowed()`. Booked holder backing is never pretransfer credit. The declared share amount is burned only when present unbooked shares cover it. Shares above the declaration are not refunded. A difference between the declaration and the whole share surplus does not by itself revert. Booked holder backing does not fill a shortfall.\"},\"returns\":{\"wethOut\":\"Amount of configured common token sent to recipient\\n     \"}},\"burnShares(uint256,address,bool)\":{\"details\":\"Called by the DETF diamond during rebasing claim token → rateAsset redemption.\\n     *      The DETF diamond handles the BPT exit and rateAsset transfer separately.\",\"params\":{\"rebasingClaimAmount\":\"Amount of rebasing claim token balance to burn\",\"owner\":\"Address whose rebasing claim token is being burned\",\"pretransferred\":\"Integrating-contract flag only. Callers with no bytecode revert `EOAPretransferNotAllowed()`. Booked holder backing is never pretransfer credit. The declared share amount is burned only when present unbooked shares cover it. Shares above the declaration are not refunded. A difference between the declaration and the whole share surplus does not by itself revert. Booked holder backing does not fill a shortfall.\"},\"returns\":{\"sharesBurned\":\"Amount of underlying shares burned\\n     \"}},\"transferHeldToken(address,address,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"PRD LOCK: rebasing package holds protocol LP; DETF pulls before burn/claim unwind.\\n     \"},\"previewExchangeOut(address,address,uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"tokenIn\":\"The token provided to the vault for an exchange.\",\"tokenOut\":\"The token the caller wishes to receive in exchange for `tokenIn`.\",\"amountOut\":\"The amount of `tokenOut` the caller wishes to receive in exchange for `tokenIn`.\"},\"returns\":{\"amountIn\":\"The amount of `tokenIn` the caller will need to provide in exchange for `amountOut` of `tokenOut`.\"},\"custom:selector\":\"0xdb149bc5\\n     \"},\"exchangeOut(address,uint256,address,uint256,address,bool,uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"tokenIn\":\"The token provided to the vault for an exchange.\",\"maxAmountIn\":\"The maximum amount of `tokenIn` the caller is willing to provide.\",\"tokenOut\":\"The token the caller wishes to receive in exchange for `tokenIn`.\",\"amountOut\":\"The amount of `tokenOut` the caller wishes to receive in exchange for `tokenIn`.\",\"recipient\":\"The address to receive the `tokenOut` tokens.\",\"pretransferred\":\"Integrating-contract flag only. The caller must transfer and consume atomically; staged use is at integrator risk with no ownership or timing guarantee. Callers with no bytecode revert `EOAPretransferNotAllowed()`. Unrecorded balance across transactions may be consumed by the next contract caller. Booked holder backing is never pretransfer credit. Exact-output refunds only `min(unrecorded balance, maxAmountIn) - used`. Amounts above `maxAmountIn` are never refunded. False-flag exact-output pulls quoted used and refunds nothing.\"},\"returns\":{\"amountIn\":\"The amount of `tokenIn` the caller has provided in exchange for `amountOut` of `tokenOut`.\"},\"custom:selector\":\"0x612d4427\\n     \"},\"previewExchangeIn(address,uint256,address)\":{\"params\":{\"tokenIn\":\"The token provided to the vault for an exchange.\",\"amountIn\":\"The amount of `tokenIn` the users wishes to exchange for `tokenOut`.\",\"tokenOut\":\"The token the caller wishes to receive in exchange for `tokenIn`.\"},\"returns\":{\"amountOut\":\"The amount of `tokenOut` the caller will receive in exchange for `amountIn` of `tokenIn`.\",\"amountRefunded\":\"The amount of `tokenIn` returned to the caller.\"},\"custom:selector\":\"0x89d61912\\n     \"},\"exchangeIn(address,uint256,address,uint256,address,bool,uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"tokenIn\":\"The token provided to the vault for an exchange.\",\"amountIn\":\"The amount of `tokenIn` the users wishes to exchange for `tokenOut`.\",\"tokenOut\":\"The token the caller wishes to receive in exchange for `tokenIn`.\",\"minAmountOut\":\"The minimum amount of `tokenOut` the caller is willing to accept.\",\"recipient\":\"The address to receive the `tokenOut` tokens.\",\"pretransferred\":\"Integrating-contract flag only. The caller must transfer and consume atomically; staged use is at integrator risk with no ownership or timing guarantee. Callers with no bytecode revert `EOAPretransferNotAllowed()`. Unrecorded balance across transactions may be consumed by the next contract caller. Booked holder backing is never pretransfer credit. The declared input is processed only when present unbooked input covers it. Tokens above the declaration are not refunded. A difference between the declaration and the whole surplus does not by itself revert. Booked inventory does not fill a shortfall.\"},\"returns\":{\"amountOut\":\"The amount of `tokenOut` the caller has received in exchange for `amountIn` of `tokenIn`.\",\"amountRefunded\":\"The amount of `tokenIn` returned to the caller.\"},\"custom:selector\":\"0x05562cc8\\n     \"},\"name()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the name of the token.\\n     \"},\"symbol()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the symbol of the token.\\n     \"},\"decimals()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the decimals places of the token.\\n     \"},\"totalSupply()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the value of tokens in existence.\\n     \"},\"balanceOf(address)\":{\"details\":\"Returns the value of tokens owned by `account`.\\n     \"},\"transfer(address,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Moves a `value` amount of tokens from the caller's account to `to`.\\n     *\\n     * Returns a boolean value indicating whether the operation succeeded.\\n     *\\n     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\\n     \"},\"allowance(address,address)\":{\"details\":\"Returns the remaining number of tokens that `spender` will be\\n     * allowed to spend on behalf of `owner` through {transferFrom}. This is\\n     * zero by default.\\n     *\\n     * This value changes when {approve} or {transferFrom} are called.\\n     \"},\"approve(address,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Sets a `value` amount of tokens as the allowance of `spender` over the\\n     * caller's tokens.\\n     *\\n     * Returns a boolean value indicating whether the operation succeeded.\\n     *\\n     * IMPORTANT: Beware that changing an allowance with this method brings the risk\\n     * that someone may use both the old and the new allowance by unfortunate\\n     * transaction ordering. One possible solution to mitigate this race\\n     * condition is to first reduce the spender's allowance to 0 and set the\\n     * desired value afterwards:\\n     * https://github.com/ethereum/EIPs/issues/20#issuecomment-263524729\\n     *\\n     * Emits an {Approval} event.\\n     \"},\"transferFrom(address,address,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Moves a `value` amount of tokens from `from` to `to` using the\\n     * allowance mechanism. `value` is then deducted from the caller's\\n     * allowance.\\n     *\\n     * Returns a boolean value indicating whether the operation succeeded.\\n     *\\n     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\\n     \"}},\"author\":\"cyotee doge <not_cyotee@proton.me>\",\"details\":\"Combines all interfaces that the rebasing claim token Diamond implements.\\n \",\"events\":{\"EIP712DomainChanged()\":{\"details\":\"MAY be emitted to signal that the domain could have changed.\\n     \"},\"Transfer(address,address,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when `amount` tokens are moved from one account (`from`) to\\n     * another (`to`).\\n     *\\n     * Note that `amount` may be zero.\\n     \"},\"Approval(address,address,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when the allowance of a `spender` for an `owner` is set by\\n     * a call to {approve}. `amount` is the new allowance.\\n     \"}},\"errors\":{\"MaxAmountExceeded(uint256,uint256)\":[{\"details\":\"Error thrown when the maximum allowed amount is exceeded\",\"params\":{\"maxAmount\":\"The maximum allowed amount\",\"requiredAmount\":\"The required amount that exceeded the maximum\\n     \"}}],\"InvalidRoute(address,address)\":[{\"details\":\"Error thrown when an invalid token route is attempted\",\"params\":{\"tokenIn\":\"The input token address\",\"tokenOut\":\"The output token address\\n     \"}}]},\"title\":\"IRebasingClaimTokenProxy\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"sharesOf(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the underlying shares owned by an account.\"},\"totalShares()\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the total underlying shares.\"},\"redemptionRate()\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the current redemption rate (zapout of reserve LP per claim share).\"},\"detf()\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the DETF diamond.\"},\"setDetf(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Sets the DETF contract used for pricing and redemption callbacks.\"},\"detfNFTId()\":{\